<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moca, Dominican Republic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moca is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cibao">Cibao</a> valley of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>, capital of Espaillat Province. In 1805 Haitian forces retreating from their siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-christophe">Henri Christophe</a> sacked the town and killed many of its inhabitants. In 1899 the dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulises-heureaux">Ulises Heureaux</a> was assassinated there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moca-dominican-republic.jpg" alt="Moca, Dominican Republic" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mercedes Ramirez Guerrero · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iglesia_Sagrado_Corazon_de_Jesus_Moca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
